    "final_answer": "I have all the information needed. Let me record the findings:\n\n## Answer\n\nBased on browsing Hugging Face's Daily Papers page, here are the details for the **#1 Paper of the day**:\n\n### 📄 Title\n**\"Training Object Permanence in World Models\"**\n\n- **Authors**: Haotian Zhang, Fengyuan Yu, Dezhi Luo, and many others (from Carnegie Mellon University)\n- **Submitted by**: Hokin Deng\n- **Published on**: Sep 23, 2026\n- **arXiv ID**: 2609.28654\n- **Abstract summary**: The paper introduces WROP (World Reasoning with Object Permanence), a data infrastructure of 150 hand-designed cognitive science-inspired tasks, and presents PWM-WROP, a 16B world model. The paper was ranked #1 Paper of the day.\n\n### 👍 Upvotes\n**196 upvotes**\n\n### 🎯 Related Model / Data Releases\nYes, the paper is accompanied by several related releases on Hugging Face:\n\n| Type | Count | Name |\n|---|---|---|\n| **Models** | 1 | `Hokin/PWM-WROP` — a 15B parameter Video-to-Video model |\n| **Datasets** | 2 | `Hokin/object-permanence` and `Hokin/object-permanence-benchmark` |\n| **Spaces** | 1 | `hugging-apps/pwm-wrop-object-permanence` |\n\nSo the authors (Hokin) have released both the **model** (PWM-WROP, a 15B-parameter video world model) and **two datasets** (the object-permanence training data and benchmark) along with a demo Space, providing full reproducibility for their research.",
